WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.130 line:78% position:50% align:center
The deepest ocean could
swallow Mount Everest.

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:06.820 line:78% position:50% align:center
After 200 meters,
sunlight is already fading.

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:10.250 line:78% position:50% align:center
At 1,000 meters,
it disappears.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:15.400 line:78% position:50% align:center
The average ocean is nearly
3.7 kilometers deep.

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:19.170 line:78% position:50% align:center
Now place Mount Everest
on the bottom.

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:23.920 line:78% position:50% align:center
Its summit would still be more than
two kilometers underwater.

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:30.420 line:78% position:50% align:center
Challenger Deep.
Nearly 11 kilometers below the surface.
